59
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:26.220
We could make it to where, you know use the best parts

60
00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:29.640
of whatever he did and make it good.

61
00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.470
But honestly, most of it was from one take,

62
00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.930
which is impressive.

63
00:02:33.930 --> 00:02:38.930
Is that now one of those memories that just lives on?

64
00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:41.320
Yes, I mean, I've told everybody,

65
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.510
I was like, I don't know how cooperative he's gonna be,

66
00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.790
I don't know if he's gonna (indistinct) go once and be like

67
00:02:46.790 --> 00:02:48.400
I don't wanna do this anymore,

68
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.320
but if nothing else I have this moment,

69
00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.540
I have this day he got to come to work with me

70
00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.600
and see what I do.

71
00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.180
And it was such a magical experience in the studio.

72
00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.170
But then having that moment

73
00:03:00.170 --> 00:03:05.170
ingrained forever in a musical form, his little voice.

74
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.620
He already pronounces his rums.

75
00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.700
Like, just from that point to this point,

76
00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:12.670
he doesn't say pauampompompom anymore.

77
00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.220
He says, Parapampampam.

78
00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:17.350
And it's like that was such a fleeting moment,

79
00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.590
it's not there anymore

80
00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:21.890
and I have that forever.

81
00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:22.830
It's so true.

82
00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.270
Like my kids, if they come visit me at work

83
00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.480
I don't know what version of them I'm getting that day.

84
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.300
