94
00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.437
and John Candy looks at him, he goes,

95
00:04:00.437 --> 00:04:02.921
"Yeah, those moments don't come around again."

96
00:04:02.921 --> 00:04:05.170
(laughing)

97
00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:09.350
Okay, I have to ask you about organization.

98
00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:14.210
I hear you're a fan of organization

99
00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:18.790
and it wasn't my forte growing up,

100
00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.900
I was like pig pen and I lost everything

101
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.260
and I was just Bohemian and whimsical

102
00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.930
and now I'm really trying to be a different person.

103
00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:30.770
What are your tips for organizing?

104
00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:34.700
What is Carrie Underwood's tips for organizing?

105
00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.700
I mean, I feel like it's important to focus on one thing.

106
00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.420 line:15%
I feel like if I walk into my kitchen,

107
00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.790 line:15%
my kitchen is overwhelming.

108
00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:46.600 line:15%
If I just walk into my pantry

109
00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:48.890 line:15%
and like that is what I'm taking charge of,

110
00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:50.980 line:15%
that is what I'm organizing.

111
00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:53.610 line:15%
I feel like that is, it is doable.

112
00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:57.650 line:15%
It is one space, work on one space, one drawer,

113
00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.990
one little area.

114
00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.870
Don't just go in because then you feel

115
00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.460
like you haven't done anything.

116
00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:03.850
You could work all day

117
00:05:03.850 --> 00:05:06.950
and if you're just Willy nilly, putting stuff away

118
00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.800
you feel like you haven't really gotten any accomplished.

119
00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.770
You don't see it in front of you.

120
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:13.650
If you work on one drawer, one pantry, one thing

121
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.520
then that's doable.

122
00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.450
And then sometimes I feel like taking things out,

123
00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:19.670
like taking all of it out

124
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.660
and putting it back in the way it should go

125
00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.103
is helpful instead of just moving things around.

126
00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:30.543 line:15%
And while you're doing that, you can throw things away.

127
00:05:32.295 --> 00:05:33.730 line:15%
You gotta be brutal, let it go.

128
00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.290 line:15%
If you're not gonna use it, if it doesn't serve your purpose

129
00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:37.380 line:15%
if you're not gonna eat it,

130
00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.790 line:15%
if you're not gonna like whatever.

131
00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:43.690 line:15%
You have worn it in you know, a year, like just let it go.

132
00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.370
My therapist (indistinct),

133
00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.040
because I have a time management thing

134
00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:47.980
I'm trying to conquer.

135
00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.480
He was like, you need to be ruthless on yourself.

136
00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.490
And that's a word that's really stuck with me

137
00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:55.700
and haunted me.
Because you feel

138
00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.740
so much lighter afterwards

139
00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.790
when you get rid of, when you purge

140
00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.540
and then all the things that you need

141
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.290
are right in front of you,

142
00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.720
you can breathe, it just feels better.

143
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.387
There's someone who said this saying,

144
00:06:08.387 --> 00:06:10.730
"Your head is as messy as your room is."

145
00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:13.650
And it just was the light bulb

146
00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:17.380
and I heard you even like make your bed every morning.

147
00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.230 line:15%
Yeah, I mean, that's, if I don't have time,

148
00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:21.063 line:15%
I don't have time.

149
00:06:21.063 --> 00:06:24.100 line:15%
But when I walk by my room, if I'm there in my house

150
00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.420 line:15%
and I walk by my room and my bed is in shambles,

151
00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:29.610 line:15%
I'm like, it just irks me every time I walk by it.

152
00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.640 line:15%
So at some point I have to stop and I have to make it.

153
00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.120 line:15%
And then each time I walk by, I feel good.

154
00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.570
Well, it's funny, 'cause I read

155
00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:39.350
that you like to make your bed

156
00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.767
and when the person said

157
00:06:40.767 --> 00:06:42.740
"your head is as messy as your room is",

158
00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:45.050
a starting place for me was the bed.

159
00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.940
And it became symbolic of like, I start the day this way

160
00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:52.630
that intention might carry me through other areas.

161
00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.720
Well, and it's the kind of thing that it's like,

162
00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:57.090
okay, does this take me that long to do?

163
00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:59.240
No, like just do it and get it over with,

164
00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.450
and then get on with your life.

165
00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:03.100
And that's how I look at, you know, working out

166
00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.630
and taking care of myself too.

167
00:07:05.630 --> 00:07:08.580
Just get it done, get up, go to the gym,

168
00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:10.420
then you've done it, it's over.

169
00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.550
You feel better, you're doing something good for yourself.

170
00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.780
And you think about, it's just making your bed,

171
00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:17.270
